   "summary": "This portion of the consolidated report on Tokushima Prefecture opens with the table of contents and an introduction detailing the scope, methodology, and administrative control structure of Japanese education prior to the 6-3-3-4 system reform. It presents twelve summary statistical tables analyzing institutions, student enrollments, and teacher numbers across national, prefectural, municipal, town/village, and private jurisdictions as of April 30 and November 30, 1946. The remainder contains Part Three's detailed directory roster listing national colleges and normal schools, prefectural middle and vocational schools, municipal schools, and town/village youth and elementary schools along with their founding dates, locations, enrollments, and teaching staff.",
